": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"74\\\") (name \\\"FLOAT_HIGH\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"C5\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") ...) (node (ref \\\"R9\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") ...)\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(name \\\"+3V3\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"C5\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"C5 FLOAT_HIGH +3V3 100n\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"C4 0 FLOAT_LOW 100n\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The high-level float input is filtered against the 3.3 V rail instead of ground, so its debounce and noise filtering do not work as intended. The float-high sensor (overflow protection) may read incorrectly during transients.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.4\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"wrong_connection\",\n      \"components\": [\"R5\", \"R1\", \"T1\", \"T2\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"R5.1\", \"R5.2\", \"T2.1\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"/G_PUMP\" , \"+3V3\", \"PUMP_MAIN\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The main pump's gate net G_PUMP is pulled up to +3V3 through R5 (10k). Its pre-driver T1 is the only path pulling the gate low. Every other low-side switch gate in this design (ATO via R12, and the main-pump drive path) is pulled to GND.\",\n      \"expected\": \"A low-side N-MOSFET gate should be pulled down to GND by default so the pump stays off at power-up and during reset. Pulling the gate to +3V3 makes the 24 V pump default to ON whenever the MCU pin is high-impedance.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"46\\\") (name \\\"/G_{PUMP}\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"R5\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") ...) ... (node (ref \\\"T2\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"G\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"R5 /GPUMP +3V3 10k\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"75\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"R12\\\") ...)\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The main circulation pump may run unintentionally at boot or on MCU reset, which is a safety and operational concern for a nutrient-recirculation system.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist shows a value/part-metadata mismatch on C32 (100p labelled on a 100 nF part), a float-switch filter capacitor C5 returned to +3V3 rather than GND in a mirror of C4, and a main-pump gate pulled up to +3V3 (R5) rather than pulled down. The first two are the most likely genuine deviations; the third is a design-judgment question.\"\n}",
